          "com.anthropic.claude-code-url-handler"
        ]
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "manual",
          "text": "Optional, not auto-applied: DISABLE_ERROR_REPORTING=1 and CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_FEEDBACK_SURVEY=1 (in ~/.claude/settings.json env) are safe. Do NOT use DISABLE_TELEMETRY / DO_NOT_TRACK / CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC — they disable feature flags and break Remote Control."
        }
      ],
      "source": "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/data-usage",
      "note": "Usage metrics can't be turned off without losing Remote Control (deliberate exception, see rc.d/85-functions.zsh). Opt-out vars trigger on any non-empty value, even 0.",
